        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1273" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-990" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="3760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1274" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-990" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Constitutional Blueprint&quot; and Policy Payload&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;specification.rs&lt;/code&gt; defines the formal structure of a Policy. It acts as the final gatekeeper, ensuring that every legal document loaded into the system is structurally sound, version-compliant, and logically coherent before it ever touches the execution engine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Blueprint:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Atomic Validity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;A &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;19&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; is treated as a single atomic unit. The validation logic ensures that a policy cannot exist in a &quot;partial&quot; or &quot;broken&quot; state—if the ID is missing, a rule ID is duplicated, or a currency tag is malformed, the entire document is rejected at the threshold.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Versioned Authority:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;By embedding &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;34&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;PolicySchemaVersion&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the system is future-proofed. The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;89&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;validate()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; method acts as a version-gate, preventing the engine from attempting to execute &quot;laws&quot; from a future or incompatible schema.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Human-Readable Auditability:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;33&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;PolicyMetadata&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; provides the &quot;why&quot; and &quot;who&quot; behind the &quot;how&quot;. While the engine ignores these fields during execution, they are critical for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;177&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BARD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (UI/UX) layer to explain the law to the user.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Resource Efficiency:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Through clever use of Serde attributes, the binary and text footprints of policies are kept to a minimum. Only the active constraints are serialized, making the system ideal for low-latency communication with auto-repair servers or ZK-provers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Recurrence Logic:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Weekday Masking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Integrated via the schedule, allowing the policy blueprint to define weekly recurring validity (7-bit mask).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;UTC Daytime Bands:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Enables &quot;Maintenance Windows&quot; or &quot;Trading Hours&quot; to be baked directly into the document structure with cross-midnight support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Month-Day Filtering:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Provides a structural hook for monthly cycles (e.g., payroll, audits, or governance votes) within the atomic policy document.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="3840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
