        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-126" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;mint.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="759" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-127" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="759" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-128" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Sovereign Syntax&quot; — Compiler Throughput &amp;amp; Query Latency&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; hierarchy, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;mint&lt;/code&gt; benchmark measures the speed of the &quot;Laws of Reality.&quot; Since MINT is the language that defines how the sovereign state functions, the latency of its compiler and lexer dictates how fast the system can internalize new rules or validate existing logic. By utilizing a query-based architecture (Salsa), we ensure that truth is not just calculated, but remembered and incrementally updated.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of Sovereign Syntax Benchmarking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Lexical Analysis Velocity (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;token_count&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This measures the raw speed of the MINT lexer as it transforms high-level &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;115&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; syntax into atomic tokens. It is the baseline for all higher-level semantic analysis, ensuring that the system can &quot;read&quot; its own laws at the speed of the CPU cache.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Query Database Overhead (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;25&quot;&gt;RiceDatabase&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The benchmark evaluates the cost of initializing and managing the Salsa query engine. This ensures that the infrastructure required for incremental computation—tracking dependencies and caching results—does not introduce parasitic lag that outweighs its benefits during small updates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Incremental Integrity Verification:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By benchmarking the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;56&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;SourceFile&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; creation and querying process, we verify that the bridge between raw source code and the internal query-based representation is fluid. This ensures that the system can react to changes in its own ruleset with sub-microsecond precision.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Zero-State&quot; Cold Start:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The current suite focuses on the &quot;Cold Start&quot; performance, providing a worst-case scenario metric. This guarantees that even in total failure and reboot, the sovereign machine can re-verify its core axioms without waiting for a &quot;warm&quot; cache.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="481" width="600" x="120" y="839" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-120" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shape=mxgraph.basic.document;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#39FF14;fillColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="680" x="80" y="1440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-141" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;private.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="1400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-142" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="1400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-143" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Private Sanctum&quot; — ZK Primitives &amp;amp; Cryptographic Environment&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; architecture, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;31&quot;&gt;private&lt;/code&gt; benchmark measures the cost of &quot;Invisible Truth.&quot; By focusing on the fundamental field operations of the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;144&quot;&gt;BN254&lt;/b&gt; elliptic curve, it establishes the performance floor for Zero-Knowledge operations. This ensures that the system&#39;s ability to maintain privacy and verify state transitions without revealing underlying data is not just cryptographically secure, but computationally viable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of Private Sanctum Benchmarking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Environment Probe Latency (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;rice_zk_environment&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This measures the overhead of initializing the Zero-Knowledge execution context. It ensures that the transition from standard execution to a &quot;Provable&quot; state is instantaneous, allowing the system to toggle privacy features without interrupting the user&#39;s flow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Algebraic Field Efficiency (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;FrBn254&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The core of ZK-SNARKs lies in modular arithmetic over large prime fields. Benchmarking the construction of field elements (scalars) ensures that the underlying library (likely &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;214&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;arkworks&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or similar) is correctly optimized for the host architecture, preventing &quot;Arithmetic Lag&quot; during complex proof generation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Scaling Foundation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;While currently testing basic construction, this suite provides the baseline for measuring future Groth16 or Plonk proof generations. It ensures that the &quot;Atomic Atoms&quot; of your privacy layer are healthy before the system attempts to build complex cryptographic &quot;Molecules.&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic Privacy Overheads:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By measuring these primitives, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;68&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Builder&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; can guarantee that the privacy layer&#39;s performance is deterministic. This is essential for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;171&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Clerk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to calculate gas costs or execution time limits for private contracts without the risk of timeouts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="480" width="600" x="120" y="1480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-119" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shape=mxgraph.basic.document;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#39FF14;fillColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="680" x="80" y="2080" as="geometry" />
