          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="3320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-131" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Mathematical Sound Barrier&quot; — Cross-Kernel Logic Latency&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; id=&quot;model-response-message-contentr_be868d8e6c20a5b6&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; architecture, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;31&quot;&gt;calc&lt;/code&gt; benchmark measures the velocity of &quot;Verified Logic.&quot; Since all complex financial derivations are offloaded to the Haskell-based &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;164&quot;&gt;CALC&lt;/b&gt; engine for formal correctness, the latency of this bridge determines the maximum transaction throughput of the entire system. This suite ensures that the transition between the high-performance Rust &quot;muscle&quot; and the high-integrity Haskell &quot;brain&quot; is as fluid as possible.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of Mathematical Sound Barrier Benchmarking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;FFI Bridge Overhead (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;21&quot;&gt;calc_bps_fee_json&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This measures the raw cost of crossing the boundary between Rust and Haskell. It includes the time taken to marshal data, switch execution contexts (GHC context switching), and return the result. By keeping this in the low microsecond range, the system ensures that formal verification doesn&#39;t stall the real-time execution path.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Serialization &amp;amp; Schema Validation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The benchmark accounts for the overhead of encoding and decoding the communication format (likely JSON or a similar minor-unit string format). This is the &quot;Tax on Safety&quot;—the price paid to ensure that both kernels agree on the exact decimal precision of every fee calculation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic Runtime Stability:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By running these benchmarks on Unix-specific paths with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;89&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;calc-bench&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; enabled, we monitor the stability of the Haskell runtime under high-frequency call patterns. It ensures that the GHC garbage collector doesn&#39;t introduce &quot;Stop-the-World&quot; pauses during critical financial calculations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Feature-Gated Validation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The use of conditional compilation (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;62&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;#[cfg]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;) ensures that the production binary remains lean. The benchmark code only exists when explicitly summoned, adhering to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;192&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Zero-Footprint&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; principle: we only pay for the &quot;Scaffolding&quot; during the measurement phase, never in the &quot;Sovereign Build.&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="480" width="600" x="120" y="3400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-116" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shape=mxgraph.basic.document;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#39FF14;fillColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="680" x="80" y="4000" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-132" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;security.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="3960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-133" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="3960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-134" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Titanium Reflex&quot; — Security Overhead &amp;amp; Subprocess Integrity&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; architecture, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;31&quot;&gt;security&lt;/code&gt; benchmark measures the &quot;Weight of the Armor.&quot; For a system to be truly sovereign, its security reflexes must be fast enough to be invisible. By benchmarking the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;201&quot;&gt;Zig Warden&lt;/b&gt; hooks and the autonomous stress suite, we ensure that our titanium pancerz provides maximum protection with sub-nanosecond friction, allowing the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;358&quot;&gt;CLERK&lt;/b&gt; to operate at full throttle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of Titanium Reflex Benchmarking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Warden Logic Velocity (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;23&quot;&gt;warden_check&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;This measures the raw speed of the limit-checking logic implemented in Zig. Since these checks occur on the &quot;Hot Path&quot; of every leverage calculation, they must be faster than the Rust logic they protect. This ensures that safety is a &quot;Zero-Cost&quot; feature of the system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Autonomous Stress Validation (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;30&quot;&gt;run_security_stress_test&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;By invoking the full Zig stress suite from within the Rust benchmark, the system verifies that all security invariants (memory wiping, process reaping, pressure sensing) are functioning in the current build. It’s a &quot;Live Fire&quot; exercise for the kernel’s reflexes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Compiler-to-Runtime Integration (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;33&quot;&gt;smoke_zig_smoke&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;This unique benchmark measures the health of the entire toolchain. By executing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;131&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;zig build test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the system proves that the sovereign code is not just performant, but buildable and logically sound across language boundaries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic Leverage Guard:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;34&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;check_leverage_limit&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; benchmark provides empirical evidence that our boundary protection is constant-time. This prevents &quot;Timing Side-Channel&quot; attacks where an adversary might try to deduce financial limits based on how long the security check takes to execute.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="479" width="600" x="120" y="4041" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-115" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shape=mxgraph.basic.document;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#39FF14;fillColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="640" width="680" x="80" y="4640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-135" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;lib.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="4600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-136" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="4600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-137" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-1030" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Sovereign Orchestrator&quot; — Centralized Telemetry &amp;amp; LSP Integration&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; ecosystem, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;lib.rs&lt;/code&gt; of the bench suite acts as the &quot;Sovereign Orchestrator.&quot; It unifies the disparate defensive and logical modules into a single telemetry stream. By providing a standardized &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;207&quot;&gt;BenchRow&lt;/code&gt; structure and a JSON-serialized snapshot, it enables the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;273&quot;&gt;.rice-lsp&lt;/b&gt; and other system tools to visualize the performance health of the entire Dual Kernel in real-time. This is the bridge between raw nanoseconds and actionable architectural insights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Sovereign Orchestrator:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Unified Telemetry Schema (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;26&quot;&gt;BenchRow&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By defining a strict, serializable format for all performance data, the Orchestrator ensures that whether a measurement comes from the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;172&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Haskell CALC&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; bridge or the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;199&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Zig Warden&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, it is treated with the same analytical rigor. This allows for cross-module performance correlation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Dual-Mode Diagnostics (Criterion vs. Smoke):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The system supports both &quot;Scientific Grade&quot; (Criterion) and &quot;Operational Grade&quot; (Smoke) benchmarks. This allows the developer to toggle between high-precision laboratory testing and lightning-fast &quot;Pre-Flight&quot; checks required for real-time LSP feedback.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;LSP Integration &amp;amp; Real-Time Feedback:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;42&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;--json-smoke&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; flag transforms the benchmark suite into a live data provider for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;125&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; development environment. It enables features like &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;181&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;rice.refreshBasePerf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, allowing the creator to see the performance impact of their changes without leaving the flow of imagination.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Conditional Feature Mapping:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The Orchestrator intelligently handles optional native stacks (Haskell/Zig). It ensures that the benchmark suite remains buildable even in restricted environments, while providing &quot;Full-Native&quot; visibility when the sovereign hardware is fully engaged.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Encapsulated Dependency Management:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By mapping specific paths (like &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;68&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;util.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;80&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;mint.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;), the Orchestrator maintains a clean boundary between the benchmarking harness and the production logic. It ensures that the telemetry layer remains an invisible observer, not a participant in the system&#39;s runtime logic.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="4680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
