        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-295" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-292" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#39FF14;dashed=1;dashPattern=12 12;" value="&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 180%; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;The Machine-Grade Build Manifest&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Purpose:&lt;/b&gt; The low-level build script generated by &lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Hpack&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; white-space: pre; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;that the GHC compiler uses to assemble the binary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Target Diversity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; This file defines how the code is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;split into three distinct entities: the core &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;97&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Library&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;110&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Test Suite&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;, and the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;130&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Foreign Library&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Foreign-Library Bridge (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;rice_calc_ffi&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;type: native-shared&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; This is the most critical&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;setting. It tells Haskell to compile itself into a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;98&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;.so&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; or&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;105&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;.dll&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; file so that the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;127&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Rust UTIL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; crate can &quot;reach in&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;and call Haskell functions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;-fPIC&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; Generates &quot;Position Independent Code,&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;a requirement for creating shared libraries that can&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;be linked into your sovereign OS.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;-threaded&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; Enables the multi-threaded GHC runtime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;This ensures that when the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,1,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;78&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;CLERK&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; is doing heavy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;math, it doesn&#39;t freeze the rest of the system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Audit-Ready Testing (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;21&quot;&gt;clerk-calc-test&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Defines the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;51&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;exitcode-stdio-1.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; interface,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;allowing your CI/CD and the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;109&quot; style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;BENCH&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; module to verify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;the integrity of the math logic before any code&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;is deployed to the &quot;hot path.&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;white-space: pre; line-height: 180%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Wire Protocol (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;15&quot;&gt;other-modules: FFI&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;white-space: pre; line-height: 180%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;The Cabal file explicitly includes the FFI and Wire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;white-space: pre; line-height: 180%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;modules in the foreign-library build, ensuring the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;white-space: pre; line-height: 180%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;communication channel between Rust (JSON/Binary)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;white-space: pre; line-height: 180%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;and Haskell is always included in the final shared object.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="280" x="580" y="159.47000000000003" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
