        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-29" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-302" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Fiscal Engine&quot; — Sovereign Logic &amp;amp; Economic Calculus&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; runtime, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;22&quot;&gt;Finance.hs&lt;/code&gt; serves as the primary intelligence layer for all economic activity. It is the &quot;Brain&quot; where abstract mathematical laws are transformed into actionable financial instruments, such as interest models, tax brackets, and fee structures. By consolidating previously fragmented modules into a single, cohesive engine, the system ensures that every fiscal decision—from AI-driven micro-transactions to complex debt amortization—is derived from a unified set of high-precision primitives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Fiscal Engine:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Currency-Tagged Reality:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;29&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Money&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; type enforces a strict link between numerical value and ISO currency codes. By utilizing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;124&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;addMoney&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the engine guarantees that the kernel remains &quot;currency-aware,&quot; preventing invalid cross-asset arithmetic at the type level and ensuring that every ledger entry is contextually accurate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Time-Value Determinism:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;32&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;compoundPeriods&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;52&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;monthlyPayment&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the engine provides deterministic tools for calculating the time value of money. These formulas allow the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;174&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; environment to handle loans, staking rewards, and inflationary adjustments without the drift or rounding errors common in non-functional financial systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Progressive Fiscal Policy:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;31&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;progressiveMarginal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; helper implements piecewise-linear tax logic. This allows the system to support complex, multi-bracket tax schedules (VAT, Income, or Protocol Surcharges) with a single, efficient fold, ensuring that fiscal policy remains as flexible as it is mathematically sound.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Audit-Ready Fee Generation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;28&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;basisPointsFee&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; is the engine&#39;s &quot;hot path.&quot; It not only calculates fees with basis-point precision but also generates a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;147&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;virtualJournalLine&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. This ensures that every calculation creates a transparent audit trail (a &quot;State Witness&quot;) compatible with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;273&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;hledger&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, bridging the gap between calculation and record-keeping.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Normalization &amp;amp; Hygiene:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By integrating &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;40&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;normalizeDecimal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;61&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;pruneEmptyTexts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the engine maintains a clean state. It ensures that output strings are stripped of redundant data and that transaction lists are free of empty artifacts, optimizing the throughput for downstream modules like &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;286&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;FFI&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;294&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Wire&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="1560" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-30" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-302" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Risk.hs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="2920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-31" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-302" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="2920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-32" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-302" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Sovereign Risk-Guard&quot; — Policy Analysis &amp;amp; Safety Hooks&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; architecture, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;Risk.hs&lt;/code&gt; serves as the proactive sentinel for the system’s financial health. Positioned between the calculation engine and the final execution layers, it acts as a decision-making filter. Its role is to evaluate the safety of proposed transactions against systemic policies, such as leverage limits and exposure caps, ensuring the runtime never enters a state of insolvency or extreme volatility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Sovereign Risk-Guard:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Non-Neutral Exposure Assessment:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;41&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;leverageRatio&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the module provides a specialized lens for viewing assets. It translates raw ledger data (exposure vs. collateral) into a unified risk metric. This allows the system to determine at any moment if a participant is &quot;neutral&quot; or over-extended, serving as the primary trigger for liquidation or safety interventions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Pre-Execution Policy Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By returning an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;50&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Either Text Text&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the Guard is designed to &quot;veto&quot; transactions. If a calculated ratio exceeds the protocol’s allowed risk parameters (caps), the module can return a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;215&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Left&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; error, effectively halting the flow of value before it reaches the FFI and impacts the ledger.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Contextual Placeholder for AI Models:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;While currently lightweight, this module is the designated entry point for real-world risk models. It provides the necessary hooks for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;173&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;SAGE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (Python/Mojo) or internal logic to inject complex volatility assessments and dynamic caps based on real-time market conditions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic Risk Signaling:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By returning decimal strings (e.g., &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;66&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&quot;1.0&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;), the module ensures that risk signals are human-readable and machine-verifiable. This allows external observers—like the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;194&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BARD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; interface—to visualize the &quot;health&quot; of the machine&#39;s state without needing to re-calculate complex internal exposures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="480" width="600" x="120" y="3000" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
