        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-37" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-304" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="48" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-38" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-304" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Mathematical Gauntlet&quot; — Property-Based Stress Testing&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; validation tier, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;30&quot;&gt;FuzzSpec.hs&lt;/code&gt; represents the most rigorous level of scrutiny. While unit tests check specific cases, the &quot;Gauntlet&quot; uses property-based testing (QuickCheck) to verify that the system’s mathematical laws hold true across millions of random inputs. It is the engine that proves the kernel is not just &quot;mostly correct,&quot; but algebraically sound, ensuring that even under extreme financial edge cases, the sovereign state remains stable.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Mathematical Gauntlet:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Algebraic Integrity (Associativity &amp;amp; Distributivity):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By subjecting &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;68&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;prop_decimalAddAssoc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;93&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;prop_decimalMulDistrib&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to thousands of iterations, the Gauntlet ensures that the underlying &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;185&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;RiceDecimal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; math is bulletproof. This guarantees that rounding or scaling operations do not introduce &quot;hidden leakage&quot; or floating-point drift, regardless of the order of calculation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Currency Invariant Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;40&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;prop_moneySameCurrencyAdd&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the spec verifies that the kernel maintains strict isolation between assets. It ensures that the system’s &quot;money laws&quot; are never violated, providing a mathematical guarantee that mismatched currencies cannot be combined, thus protecting the ledger&#39;s integrity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;High-Intensity Fuzzing (10,000 Cases):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;43&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;prop_basisPointsFeeParses&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; test is set to a &quot;Heavy&quot; mode, running 10,000 unique cases to stress-test the path between the logic engine and the data parsers. This high-density fuzzing is designed to catch rare, &quot;black swan&quot; numerical errors that would be impossible to find via manual testing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Dynamic Intensity Scaling:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By accepting &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;40&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;maxQc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; as an input (derived from environment variables), the Gauntlet allows the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;120&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; runtime to adapt its validation depth. This allows for rapid feedback during development while enabling exhaustive &quot;Sovereign Grade&quot; verification before a new version of the kernel is deployed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Atomic-to-Logic Verification:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This spec serves as the bridge between the lowest-level atoms (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;93&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Decimal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;) and the highest-level safety checks (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;139&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Verify&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;). It ensures that every foundational primitive in the kernel is resilient enough to support the complex financial processes running on the layers above.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="80" y="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-39" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-304" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;LogicSpec.hs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
