        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-44" parent="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-304" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Integrity Watchman&quot; — Audit Stability &amp;amp; Policy Verification&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the&amp;nbsp;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;test suite,&amp;nbsp;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;25&quot;&gt;AuditSpec.hs&lt;/code&gt;&amp;nbsp;serves as the guardian of system transparency and risk consistency. It focuses on the &quot;after-action report&quot; (the ledger audit trail) and the &quot;operational guardrails&quot; (risk policy). By ensuring that audit markers remain stable and risk hooks are responsive, this module guarantees that external indexers and the protocol’s safety layers can always rely on the kernel&#39;s output.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Integrity Watchman:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Audit Marker Stability:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The module verifies the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;48&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;riceCalcVirtualNote&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;formatting. This is critical for downstream indexers and sovereign observers who rely on the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;161&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;; rice-calc virtual:&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;string to filter system-generated transactions from user activity. By enforcing this stability, the Watchman ensures the audit trail remains &quot;machine-readable&quot; forever.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Namespace Domain Tagging:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Through &quot;domain tag&quot; checks, the Spec ensures that every virtual posting is correctly attributed to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;130&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;rice-calc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;kernel. This prevents ambiguity in multi-chain or multi-module environments, maintaining a clear provenance for every automated fee or adjustment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Risk Hook Baseline:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The module tests the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;41&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;leverageRatio&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;for its default &quot;Neutral&quot; state. By confirming that the initial implementation returns a predictable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;156&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Right &quot;1.0&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, it establishes a safe baseline for the protocol&#39;s risk analysis before more complex AI-driven or algorithmic models are injected.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Input Resilience:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;By passing arbitrary text to the risk engine, the Watchman verifies that the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;95&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Risk&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;module handles diverse input data without crashing. This ensures that the bridge between the kernel&#39;s financial data and its safety policies is robust and prepared for future expansion into real-time exposure monitoring.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Sovereign Transparency:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ultimately, this Spec proves that the kernel is not a &quot;black box.&quot; It demonstrates that every internal decision leaves a verifiable trace on the ledger and passes through a defined (and testable) risk-assessment gate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="80" y="1640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
