        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1164" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Pain Map&quot; and Privacy Guard of the Organism&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; id=&quot;model-response-message-contentr_be868d8e6c20a5b6&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;17&quot;&gt;private&lt;/code&gt; layer’s &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;33&quot;&gt;error.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;49&quot;&gt;Systemic Shield&lt;/b&gt;. It defines how the organism feels and reports failures within the shadows of Zero-Knowledge (ZK). It ensures that any breach in the privacy pipeline—whether a mathematical mismatch or a compliance veto—is felt with absolute precision, protecting the user&#39;s secrets from being leaked or misused by external entities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The ZK Lifecycle Taxonomy:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module categorizes &quot;pain&quot; into specific biological stages of a proof: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;101&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Field&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (atomic arithmetic), &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;128&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;R1CS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (genetic structure), &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;154&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (environmental conditions), and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;192&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Proving/Verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (muscle and sight). This allows the system to distinguish between a temporary &quot;cramp&quot; (serialization error) and a fatal &quot;genetic defect&quot; (circuit constraint violation).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Conscience&quot; Veto (Compliance):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;A unique pillar of this module is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;70&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ComplianceVeto&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. It acts as the organism&#39;s moral compass, allowing the private layer to refuse an operation if it violates the user’s flexible privacy rules. This is the mechanism that &quot;blocks the tax office&quot; or any unauthorized entity by mathematically refusing to generate a valid proof for non-compliant requests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Nullifier Integrity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module treats &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;50&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;IdentityNullifierCollision&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; as a critical immune response. By detecting and typing &quot;double-spend&quot; or &quot;replay&quot; attempts at the nerve level, it prevents the corruption of the private ledger, ensuring that shielded resources remain unique and non-forgeable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Safe Lifting (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;14&quot;&gt;into_rice&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Because the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;38&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;CLERK&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; layer (the brain) must understand private pain without seeing the private data, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;128&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;into_rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; bridge translates complex cryptographic failures into a unified vocabulary. It &quot;filters&quot; the high-level ZK noise into actionable &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;267&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;RiceError&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; signals like &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;290&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Crypto&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, ensuring the system reacts correctly while keeping the technical details of the &quot;shadow&quot; contained.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Transparent Propagation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Uses &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;30&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;#[error(transparent)]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;56&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;arkworks&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;69&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;std::io&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; errors, preserving the original mathematical context for the developer while maintaining the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;170&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; error hierarchy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Safety Invariants:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Includes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;28&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;SecretLeak&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; as a &quot;fail-closed&quot; mechanism. If an internal logic gate detects a potential mishandling of witness data, the system aborts instantly rather than risking the user’s privacy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Domain Guarding:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Explicitly handles &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;36&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;CurveMismatch&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to prevent &quot;cross-species&quot; cryptographic attacks, ensuring that BN254 logic never accidentally interacts with BLS12-381 parameters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="680" width="600" x="120" y="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1165" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;field.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1166" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1167" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Mathematical Soil&quot; and Scalar Foundation of the Organism&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;field.rs&lt;/code&gt; provides the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;35&quot;&gt;Prime Field&lt;/b&gt; substrate. If the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;65&quot;&gt;private&lt;/code&gt; layer is a shadow, these fields are the dust particles that form it. This module handles the high-speed modular arithmetic required to represent secrets (scalars) as elements of a finite field, ensuring they are mathematically compatible with the elliptic curves above them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Scalar Abstraction (Genetic Bases):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module abstracts the complexity of different prime fields (BN254 for speed, BLS12-381 for security) through the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;152&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;RiceScalar&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; trait. It provides a unified way to handle &quot;shadow scalars,&quot; allowing the rest of the system to perform math without needing to know the underlying modulus or curve specifics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Strict Canonical Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Unlike standard implementations, this module &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;75&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;rejects&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; non-canonical byte inputs. By enforcing that every field element must be strictly less than the field modulus during parsing, it prevents subtle cryptographic attacks and ensures that every secret has a single, verifiable representation on the wire.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Constant-Time Reflexes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Safety is baked into the arithmetic. Using &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;67&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;to_be_bytes_fixed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; combined with the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;103&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;util&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; layer&#39;s secure comparison, the module prevents side-channel timing attacks. The magnitude of a secret balance or identity key cannot be leaked by the time it takes to compare it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Performance Metabolism (Batching):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;To support heavy ZK operations, the module implements Montgomery’s batch inversion. This drastically reduces the computational cost of generating complex proofs (like those for private balances), allowing the &quot;organism&quot; to process multiple secret transactions with minimal latency.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Field-Agnostic API:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;24&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;RiceScalar&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; trait allows for easy expansion to new fields (e.g., Post-Quantum Lattice fields) without changing the high-level &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;149&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;private&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; logic.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Poseidon Readiness:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Built-in hooks for Poseidon hashing ensure the system is ready for hyper-efficient in-circuit state commitments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Zero-Copy Integration:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Deep integration with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;45&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;util::Bytes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; ensures that moving scalars from the network into the mathematical &quot;inner sanctum&quot; happens with zero unnecessary overhead.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="1000" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1168" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;commitment.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="3160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1169" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="3160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1170" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Immutable Vows&quot; and Anchor of Shielded State&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;commitments.rs&lt;/code&gt; provides the mechanism for &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;55&quot;&gt;binding secrecy&lt;/b&gt;. It allows the system to freeze a value (like a balance or an ID) into a public cryptographic anchor. Once committed, the value cannot be changed, yet it remains completely invisible to anyone without the original &quot;opening&quot; key.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Algebraic Commitments (Pedersen):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;By combining secret values with high-entropy blinding factors on elliptic curves, the module creates &quot;Pedersen Commitments.&quot; These are the gold standard for private accounting because they are homomorphic—you can add two commitments together to get a commitment to the sum of their values, all without ever revealing the numbers themselves.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;ZK-Optimized Hashing (Poseidon):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The module implements the Poseidon sponge function, specifically tuned for the BLS12-381 field. This is the &quot;fast lane&quot; for ZK-circuits, allowing the OS to verify identities and state transitions in milliseconds while maintaining maximum privacy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;Double-Spend Protection (Nullifiers):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;To ensure integrity in a private world, the module provides &quot;Nullifier hooks.&quot; A nullifier is a deterministic fingerprint of a commitment that can be revealed when the commitment is &quot;spent.&quot; It allows the network to prevent fraud without ever linking the transaction back to the user&#39;s permanent identity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;Sealed State Lifecycle:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;Commitments are fully integrated with the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;66&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;serial&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt; layer. They can be encrypted into &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;107&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;VaultEnvelopes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt; for secure off-chain storage or broadcast as public inputs for Groth16 proofs, acting as the bridge between private user data and public verification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Perfect Hiding:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Even an attacker with a quantum computer cannot extract the value from a Pedersen commitment without the blinding factor (statistical hiding).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212));&quot;&gt;Deterministic Verification:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;32&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;CommitmentOpening&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; struct ensures a standardized way to reveal secrets when the user chooses to, with built-in validation against the public anchors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="3240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1171" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;curve.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="1680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1172" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="1680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1173" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Adaptive Shield&quot; and Multi-Curve Geometry of the Organism&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;curve.rs&lt;/code&gt; defines the geometry of our privacy. It is the layer where abstract scalars from &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;103&quot;&gt;field.rs&lt;/code&gt; are mapped onto elliptic curves to create public keys, commitments, and proofs. This module is designed with &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;221&quot;&gt;Quantum Agility&lt;/b&gt;, meaning it doesn&#39;t just provide one type of lock, but a modular, hybrid vault system.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Quantum-Agile Hybridization:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The module introduces &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;51&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;HybridPoint&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, a dual-lane container that pairs classical Elliptic Curve points with Lattice-based (Post-Quantum) commitments. This ensures that assets can be &quot;double-locked,&quot; requiring an attacker to break two entirely different mathematical paradigms to compromise the system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Tiered Defense (Speed vs. Depth):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;By implementing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;50&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;CurveTier&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the system intelligently routes operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;105&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;DailySpeed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (BN254) is used for high-frequency, low-latency interactions, while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;184&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;DeepPrivacy&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (BLS12-381) is reserved for long-term storage and high-compliance data, offering a wider classical security margin.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Dynamic Entropy Injection (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;harden&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The module provides &quot;hardening&quot; functions that inject scalar salts into curve points. This process—mathematically consistent for pairings—adds a layer of blinding that protects against linkability and metadata analysis, effectively allowing the encryption to &quot;evolve&quot; or &quot;puchnąć&quot; under scrutiny.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Policy-Driven Verification:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Unlike rigid crypto libraries, this module integrates with the system&#39;s &quot;conscience&quot; via &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;117&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;HybridSecurityRequirement&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. It allows the organism to demand higher security levels (Hybrid) for sensitive operations, returning a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;247&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ComplianceVeto&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; if the cryptographic material doesn&#39;t meet the required quantum-resistance threshold.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Unified Pairing API:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; A single &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;30&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;RiceCurve&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; trait abstracts away the complexities of different curve families, providing a clean surface for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;137&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;e(G1, G2)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and MSM operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;MSM Efficiency:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Built-in support for Multi-Scalar Multiplication (Pippenger-style) ensures that even the most complex &quot;Post-Quantum ready&quot; proofs remain fast and energy-efficient.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Heuristic Strength Awareness:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The system is &quot;self-aware&quot; of its security bits, allowing operators to make informed decisions about curve rotation and protocol upgrades.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="640" width="600" x="120" y="1760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
