        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1176" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;The &quot;Black-Box&quot; Vault and Secret Lifecycle&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;serial.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the final gate through which private data passes to the outside world. It transforms mathematical artifacts (proofs, keys, witnesses) into &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;165&quot;&gt;RVLT (Rice Vault)&lt;/b&gt; frames—encrypted, policy-aware envelopes that enforce the user&#39;s right to digital invisibility.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Vault-Enveloped Security:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Every serialized object is wrapped in a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;66&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;VaultEnvelope&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;. This isn&#39;t just encryption; it&#39;s a &quot;Contextual Shield&quot; that binds the ciphertext to a specific &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;176&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;PolicyTag&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; (Jurisdiction) and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;205&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;QuantumSalt&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;. Even if two users generate the same proof, their encrypted outputs will be completely different and unlinked.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The &quot;Paranoid&quot; Compliance Filter:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The module implements a hard-coded &quot;Total Blackout&quot; mechanism. Through the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;109&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;ComplianceMask&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, the system can be instructed to veto any operation that attempts to move data outside the local device (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;229&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;ExternalTransmit&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;). This allows the OS to act as a rigorous filter, ensuring that &quot;private&quot; stays private.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Identity-Rooted Key Derivation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Keys are never stored; they are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;64&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;breathed into existence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;. Using a 256-bit identity root and per-message entropy, the module derives transient subkeys for the AEAD (Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data) process, ensuring maximum forward secrecy for the user&#39;s life-logs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Deterministic Integrity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;29&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;RVLT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; format is canonical and deterministic. While the encryption uses fresh randomness for safety, the outer structure is rigid, allowing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;167&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; parsers to validate the &quot;magic,&quot; versioning, and policy tags before the expensive cryptographic operations even begin.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Metadata Transparency:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;23&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;PolicyTag&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; allows for &quot;routing-only&quot; visibility—auditors can see &lt;/span&gt;&lt;i data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;87&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;which&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; rules apply to a packet without ever seeing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;i data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;137&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;what&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; is inside the packet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Fail-Closed Design:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Any mismatch in policy, any corruption of the ciphertext, or any unauthorized transmission attempt triggers an immediate &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;141&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;SecretLeak&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;155&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ComplianceVeto&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; error, halting the leak before it happens.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Zero-Knowledge Ready:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Built to handle the massive outputs of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;61&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ark-groth16&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; while keeping the wire footprint as lean as possible through canonical compression.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="520" width="600" x="120" y="2560" as="geometry" />
