        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1179" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The &quot;Primordial Keys&quot; and the Immutable Constitution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;setup.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the guardian of the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;45&quot;&gt;Common Reference String (CRS)&lt;/b&gt;. For zero-knowledge proofs to be valid, the system must operate on mathematical constants that have been verified through a trusted ceremony. This module ensures that those constants are authentic, versioned, and protected against environment-level tampering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Ceremony Integrity Guard:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Every set of parameters is bound to a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;64&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;CeremonyHash&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. This hash is a unique fingerprint of the Proving and Verifying keys combined. In production, the system performs a mandatory check: if the keys on disk don&#39;t match the hardcoded ceremony hash in the circuit definition, the OS rejects the setup, preventing &quot;Key-Injection Attacks.&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Production Lockdown:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module implements a strict environment policy. While in development it can automatically generate ephemeral keys for testing, in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;154&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;production&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; mode (triggered by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;184&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;RICE_ENV&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;), the generation logic is physically unreachable. The OS transitions into a &quot;Load-Only&quot; state, ensuring only pre-audited, ceremony-grade parameters are used.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Efficient Memory Mapping:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Recognizing that cryptographic keys can be massive, the module utilizes memory-mapping (mmap) via the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;128&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;serial&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; layer. This allows &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;154&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to handle large-scale proving circuits without bloating the system&#39;s memory footprint, enabling high-performance ZK operations even on constrained hardware.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;VkId Audit Trails:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;To simplify debugging and auditing, every &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;61&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;VerifyingKey&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; is assigned a unique &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;95&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;VkId&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. This 8-character hex string acts as a human-readable version of the privacy logic, allowing users and developers to verify they are running the correct, untampered version of the OS’s privacy protocols.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Parameter Update Authorization:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; In production, updating these keys requires explicit cryptographic authorization from the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;122&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; identity, making it impossible for malware to silently change the privacy rules.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic Persistence:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Whether cached in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;45&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;dev&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or loaded in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;62&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;prod&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the keys are stored using the canonical compression format from &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;132&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;serial.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, ensuring maximum compatibility across different architectures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="3960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1180" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;circuit.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="4640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1181" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="4640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1182" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;14&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Logical Weave&quot; and Enforcer of Hidden Truths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; id=&quot;model-response-message-contentr_be868d8e6c20a5b6&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;circuit.rs&lt;/code&gt; defines the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;36&quot;&gt;R1CS (Rank-1 Constraint System)&lt;/b&gt; that governs all private interactions. It is the mathematical blueprint that ensures honesty in a world where data is invisible. It transforms high-level concepts like &quot;ownership&quot; and &quot;solvency&quot; into a web of polynomial constraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;17,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The Balance Conservation Law:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Through the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;17,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;42&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ShieldedTransferCircuit&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the system enforces a strict zero-sum rule for every transaction. It ensures that no assets are created or destroyed in the dark, verifying that the sum of hidden inputs perfectly matches the sum of hidden outputs and public fees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;17,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Non-Negative Assurance (Range Proofs):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;One of the most critical security features, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;17,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;87&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;range_proof_u64&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; gadget, performs bit-level decomposition of hidden values. It prevents &quot;Underflow Attacks&quot; by mathematically proving that every hidden amount is a positive 64-bit integer, maintaining the economic integrity of the OS.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;17,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Anonymous Linkability (Nullifiers):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module integrates Poseidon-based nullifiers within the circuits. This allows a user to prove they are the rightful owner of a commitment and that they are &quot;consuming&quot; it, without ever revealing which specific commitment on the ledger they are using—achieving total privacy with double-spend protection.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;17,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Composable Gadgetry:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By utilizing a &quot;Gadget&quot; pattern, the circuits are built from modular, audited components. This ensures that complex logic like Poseidon hashing and bit-checks are implemented consistently across different types of proofs, from identity verification to multi-asset transfers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;18&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;18&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color&quot; style=&quot;--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;&quot; aria-live=&quot;off&quot; aria-busy=&quot;false&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;19,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BN254 Field Optimization:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Every variable is mapped to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;19,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;58&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;FrBn254&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; field, ensuring perfect compatibility with the underlying curve and the Groth16 proving system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;19,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Constraint Efficiency:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The circuits are designed to minimize the &quot;Gate Count,&quot; ensuring that even complex proofs can be generated on mobile devices or within the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;19,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;162&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; interface without lag.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="4720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1183" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;prove.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="5400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1184" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="5400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1185" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The &quot;Alchemist&#39;s Engine&quot; and the Synthesis of Anonymous Truth&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;prove.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the high-performance refinery where private data is transformed into &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;94&quot;&gt;Zero-Knowledge Proofs&lt;/b&gt;. It is the most resource-intensive part of the privacy layer, designed to be fast, observable, and fail-safe. It acts as the bridge between your secret &quot;Witness&quot; and the public &quot;Proof.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Fail-Fast&quot; Preflight Check:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Before committing CPU cycles to heavy Prover math, the module runs a &quot;Preflight&quot; simulation. It verifies the circuit constraints against the provided witness in a lightweight virtual environment. If the witness doesn&#39;t satisfy the logic, the process aborts instantly, preventing wasted energy and providing immediate feedback.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Isolated Parallelism (ZK-Rayon):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Proving is highly parallelizable. This module manages a dedicated thread pool specifically for cryptographic operations. This ensures that privacy computations utilize all available hardware power without starving other OS processes, maintaining a smooth user experience even during complex transfers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Telemetry &amp;amp; Proof Fingerprinting:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Every proving operation is instrumented with professional-grade telemetry. By generating a unique &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;132&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ProofId&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; (a 4-byte fingerprint), the OS can track, log, and debug the lifecycle of a proof across the network without ever leaking the sensitive data contained within it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Vault-Ready Integration:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Once a proof is synthesized, it is immediately prepared for the &quot;Sealed State.&quot; Using &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;111&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;seal_proof_for_vault&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the engine wraps the proof in an AEAD-encrypted envelope, ensuring that even the proof itself remains protected during transit or storage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BN254 Optimization:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Hardcoded focus on the BN254 curve ensures maximum performance for identity and transfer circuits, aligning perfectly with modern ZK-rollup standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Environment-Driven Tuning:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Parameters like batch size and thread counts are soft-coded to environment variables, allowing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;122&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to adapt its proving engine from mobile devices to high-end servers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="5480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1186" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;verify.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="6160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1187" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="6160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1188" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Silent Judge&quot; and the Immutable Verdict&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;verify.rs&lt;/code&gt; acts as the definitive arbiter of truth. It is a stateless, high-speed engine designed to validate &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;122&quot;&gt;Zero-Knowledge Proofs&lt;/b&gt; without ever needing access to the original secrets. It is the component that allows the OS to remain decentralized, as any node can verify the integrity of the state transition in milliseconds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Asymmetric Speed:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;While generating a proof is a heavy task, verification is optimized for near-instant execution. This ensures that the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;136&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; interface remains responsive even when processing complex identity claims or shielded transfers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Batch Proof Acceleration:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;To handle high-throughput scenarios, the module utilizes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;83&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Batch Verification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. By grouping multiple proofs and verifying them through a single randomized mathematical operation, the OS can scale its throughput exponentially without a linear increase in CPU cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Public Input Integrity Guard:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module enforces a strict layout check for all public inputs. By creating a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;109&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;PublicInputsFingerprint&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, it ensures that the external data provided with the proof exactly matches the parameters committed during the proving phase, preventing &quot;Transaction Malleability&quot; attacks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Parameter Store Integration:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;37&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;verify_with_store&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, the verification process is tightly coupled with the OS&#39;s trusted setup. It automatically ensures that the mathematical &quot;Judge&quot; is using the correct, audited &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;214&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;VerifyingKey&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; associated with the specific circuit version.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Pairing-Based Math:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The engine leverages &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;41&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;multi_miller_loop&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;10,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;63&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;final_exponentiation&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; on the BN254 curve, providing a robust balance between cryptographic security and execution speed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Zero-Knowledge Batching:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The random linear combination ensures that batching doesn&#39;t weaken security—an invalid proof in a batch will cause the entire batch to fail, protecting the ledger&#39;s integrity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="6240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1198" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;balance.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
