          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="6880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1203" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The &quot;Sovereign Root&quot; and the Architecture of Anonymous Trust&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;identity.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the core of user sovereignty. It manages the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;73&quot;&gt;Identity Commitment-Nullifier&lt;/b&gt; pair, which allows a user to exist within the system as a verifiable entity while remaining mathematically anonymous. It is the implementation of &quot;Privacy by Default&quot; at the biological level of the OS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The Sovereign Seed Expansion:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Identity is derived from high-entropy entropy using a robust SHA-256 expansion. This process ensures that the secret, blinding, and nullifier keys are cryptographically independent, preventing an attacker from linking one to the other even if partial data is exposed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The Nullifier Spend-Book (Double-Spend Protection):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;To ensure an identity action (like voting or rotating) happens only once, the module integrates with a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;155&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;NullifierIndex&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. By publishing a deterministic &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;201&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;IdentityNullifier&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, a user &quot;spends&quot; their right to that action, allowing the OS to prevent replay attacks without ever knowing the user&#39;s secret key.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Cryptographic Authorization Gates:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;39&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ParameterUpdateAuthorization&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; transforms identity into a functional permission. It requires a valid &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;138&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Groth16 Identity-Opening Proof&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to unlock critical system functions, such as updating the trusted-setup parameters. This ensures the OS only obeys its true owner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Vault-Sealed Attestations:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module provides a secure bridge to off-chain claims. Through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;92&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;IdentityAttestationPayload&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, users can bind verified attributes to their ZK-Commitment. These are then sealed within &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;208&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;VaultEnvelopes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, ensuring they are only revealed to authorized policies within the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;290&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; ecosystem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Poseidon-Based Commitments:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Uses the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;37&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Bn254&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; optimized Poseidon hash, ensuring that identity operations are fast enough for real-time mobile interactions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;11,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Strict Domain Separation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Every derivation and hash is tagged with a domain-specific constant, neutralizing cross-protocol attacks and ensuring cryptographic hygiene.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="6960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1204" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;compliance.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="8400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1205" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="8400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1206" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-978" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Cryptographic Notary&quot; and the Framework of Verifiable Rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;In &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;.rice OS&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;compliance.rs&lt;/code&gt; serves as the bridge between absolute privacy and the requirements of the physical or legal world. It provides the tools to prove that an identity or a transaction adheres to specific rules (Policies) without revealing any underlying personal data. By operating on the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;296&quot;&gt;BLS12-381&lt;/b&gt; curve, it ensures global compatibility with modern cryptographic standards.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Module:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Merkle Membership Proofs (The &quot;Pass&quot;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The module implements a high-performance Merkle Tree with a depth of 20. This allows users to prove their inclusion in &quot;Authorized Sets&quot; (Allow-lists) by providing an authentication path. The world sees only a valid proof against a public &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;278&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Root&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, while the user&#39;s specific identity remains hidden in the leaf.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Policy Commitment Binding:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every rule in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;45&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; ecosystem is committed to as a unique field element. Whether it&#39;s a legal contract or a system permission, the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;162&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;PolicyBinding&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; ensures that a proof generated for one specific rule cannot be reused for another, maintaining a strict &quot;one proof, one purpose&quot; integrity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Threshold &amp;amp; Quorum Logic:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Compliance often requires multi-party approval. The module natively supports &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;103&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;M-of-N&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; quorum logic, allowing the OS to require signatures or proofs from a subset of authorized &quot;Guardians&quot; before executing high-stakes operations like parameter updates or large asset mints.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Aggregated Proof Statements:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;To maintain system performance, multiple compliance checks can be compressed into a single &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;120&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;AggregatedComplianceStatement&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. This allows a transaction to carry a &quot;bundle&quot; of proofs (e.g., identity verification + regional compliance) as a single mathematical point, reducing storage costs on the ledger.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Key Technical Highlights:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BLS12-381 Interoperability:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Chosen specifically to allow &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;57&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to interact with global decentralized protocols and future-proof the OS for constant-size KZG accumulators.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;11,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Domain-Separated Hashing:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Every cryptographic operation (leaf hashing, node compression, policy commitment) is separated by a unique domain tag, neutralizing any risk of collision or cross-protocol attacks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="600" width="600" x="120" y="8480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
