        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1080" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Rhythmic Scanner&quot; — Stream Processing &amp;amp; Symbolic Extraction&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; compiler stack, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;29&quot;&gt;lexer.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the high-velocity engine that breathes life into the language. It consumes raw UTF-8 source code and, through a process of rhythmic scanning, emits a linearized stream of tokens. By applying finite-state automata logic, the lexer discards non-semantic &quot;noise&quot; such as comments and whitespace, ensuring that the downstream parser receives only the pure, crystallized essence of the financial logic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Rhythmic Scanner:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic State Transitions:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The lexer operates as a state machine that decides the identity of a token based on the current character and its lookahead. Whether it’s distinguishing a single colon &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;201&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;:&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; from a double colon &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;223&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;::&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or identifying the start of a hexadecimal address, the scanner ensures that every character is accounted for with zero ambiguity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Whitespace &amp;amp; Comment Pruning:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;To maintain a high-performance &quot;hot path&quot; for the compiler, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;90&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;lexer.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; identifies and strips out irrelevant characters. This allows the programmer to document their sovereign code extensively without impacting the complexity of the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Context-Aware Identifier Recognition:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The scanner identifies words and checks them against the &quot;Keyword Sovereignty&quot; defined in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;128&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;token.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. It serves as the primary filter that determines whether a sequence of letters is a standard variable or a reserved command that triggers protocol-level actions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;High-Fidelity Span Tracking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;As the lexer moves through the source, it continuously calculates the byte-offset, line number, and column. This data is bundled into every token, creating a &quot;geographic map&quot; of the source code that allows &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;235&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BARD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to highlight the exact location of a syntax error with pinpoint accuracy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Numeric &amp;amp; Literal Encoding:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The lexer is responsible for recognizing complex literals, such as financial decimals or time durations. It ensures that characters like &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;165&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;100.50_USD&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; are captured as a single, cohesive semantic unit, preserving the specialized notation required for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;279&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; financial ecosystem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1083" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;diagnostic.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="2960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1084" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
