        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1113" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Semantic Investigator&quot; — Cross-Reference &amp;amp; Relational Discovery&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; compilation architecture, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;39&quot;&gt;query.rs&lt;/code&gt; serves as the active search engine for the language&#39;s internal structures. While &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;129&quot;&gt;db.rs&lt;/code&gt; provides the storage, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;157&quot;&gt;query.rs&lt;/code&gt; defines the specialized &quot;questions&quot; the compiler asks to understand the relationships between different parts of a project. It is the module that handles name resolution, dependency mapping, and symbolic lookups, ensuring that when you reference a sovereign asset in one file, the system knows exactly where it was born and what rules govern it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Semantic Investigator:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Symbol Resolution &amp;amp; Binding:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module’s primary job is to link names to their definitions. It investigates the scope of a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;124&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;rule&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;132&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;asset&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, traversing the project&#39;s hierarchy to ensure that an identifier refers to the correct atomic entity, preventing ambiguity in complex financial contracts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Dependency Graph Mapping:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;26&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;query.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; identifies which modules depend on each other. By mapping these relationships, it tells the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;127&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;MINT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; compiler exactly what needs to be re-evaluated when a specific file changes, acting as the logic behind the system’s incremental speed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Type-Inquiry Interface:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;It provides the mechanism for querying the type of any expression. The evaluator or the diagnostic engine can use a query to ask, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;i data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;154&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&quot;Is this expression a Decimal or a Currency?&quot;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, allowing the system to enforce fiscal safety before execution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Usage Discovery (Find All References):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This module enables &quot;intelligence&quot; features for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;91&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BARD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; interface. It can query every location where a specific sovereign account is mentioned, allowing the developer to see the full impact of a policy change across the entire ledger.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Cross-Module Visibility Checks:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The Investigator enforces &quot;Sovereign Privacy.&quot; It determines whether a piece of logic or a data point is public, private, or restricted to a specific module, ensuring that internal financial state remains protected according to the language&#39;s visibility rules.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="5960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
