        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1116" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Topological Weaver&quot; — Dependency Mapping &amp;amp; Flow Analysis&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; compilation engine, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;33&quot;&gt;graph.rs&lt;/code&gt; is responsible for constructing the &quot;Social Map&quot; of the code. While the AST is a simple hierarchy, the Graph is a complex web of directed relationships. It identifies how data, assets, and permissions flow between different sovereign modules. By representing the system as a mathematical graph (nodes and edges), it allows the compiler to detect circular dependencies, analyze the impact of changes, and visualize the entire financial ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Topological Weaver:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Directional Dependency Resolution:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module builds a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) of the project. It ensures that if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;119&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Asset A&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; depends on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;138&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Rule B&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, there are no &quot;infinite loops&quot; where &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;182&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Rule B&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; also depends on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;205&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Asset A&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. This prevents the system from entering an unstable state during compilation or execution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Value-Flow Visualization:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;26&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;graph.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; maps the path of &quot;Value&quot; through the system. It tracks how a decimal amount moves from a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;124&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;mint&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; block through various &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;151&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;rules&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; into a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;164&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;ledger&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;. This graph provides the data necessary for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;215&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;BARD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to generate a visual &quot;Financial Flow&quot; diagram for the user.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Sovereign Impact Analysis:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;By traversing the graph, the compiler can perform &quot;What-If&quot; analysis. It can determine exactly which contracts or ledgers will be affected if a specific root policy is modified, acting as a safety simulation tool before any code is &quot;committed&quot; to the state.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Dead-Node Detection:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The graph identifies &quot;Orphaned Logic&quot;—parts of the code that are defined but never reached or utilized. This allows the compiler to prune unnecessary nodes, ensuring the resulting bytecode or machine instructions are as lean and efficient as possible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Cross-Module Linkage:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;In a multi-file &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;38&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; project, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;53&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;graph.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; acts as the bridge. it connects local AST nodes to external symbols resolved by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;142&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;query.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;, creating a unified, global map of the entire sovereign machine.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="6680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1119" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;lower.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="80" y="8040" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1120" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="88" y="8040" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NetWeRefARGaiRHp-jNh-1121" parent="buZBv7jyl6kujNXGrouv-966" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Instruction Translator&quot; — High-to-Low Semantic Reduction&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; compilation pipeline, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;35&quot;&gt;lower.rs&lt;/code&gt; is the bridge between human imagination and machine execution. Its purpose is to perform &quot;Lowering&quot;: the process of deconstructing high-level, complex language constructs (like nested &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;228&quot;&gt;rule&lt;/code&gt; blocks or sovereign &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;253&quot;&gt;mint&lt;/code&gt; declarations) into a simpler, intermediate representation (IR). By breaking down &quot;syntactic sugar&quot; into a series of primitive operations, this module prepares the code for final optimization and hardware-level execution.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of the Instruction Translator:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;De-Sugaring Complex Syntax:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The module takes elegant, high-level code and reduces it to its most basic functional components. For example, a complex &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;149&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;if-else&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; financial rule might be &quot;lowered&quot; into simple conditional jumps and basic arithmetic, making it ready for a virtual machine or CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Canonical Representation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;26&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;lower.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; ensures that multiple ways of writing the same thing in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;95&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; language end up as the same simplified instruction. This &quot;canonicalization&quot; simplifies the work for the backend, as it only has to understand a small set of primitive commands.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Memory &amp;amp; Storage Mapping:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This is where abstract variable names start to become concrete memory offsets or database keys. The module decides how a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;147&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Decimal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; value or a sovereign &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;176&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Account&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; is physically represented in the system&#39;s runtime memory.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Flow Flattening:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The hierarchical tree structure of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;56&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;AST&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; is &quot;flattened&quot; into a linear sequence of instructions. This process removes the nesting of the source code and turns it into a straight line of execution steps that the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;229&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; kernel can follow without ambiguity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Constraint Simplification:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Financial invariants and safety checks defined in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;6,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;77&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;check.rs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; are lowered into runtime assertions. The module ensures that the &quot;Sovereign Laws&quot; of the code are translated into actual machine-level checks that guard every transaction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="560" width="600" x="120" y="8120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
