        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-123" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeWidth=2;align=right;strokeColor=#39FF14;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;util.rs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="680" x="3680" y="-26920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-124" parent="1" style="verticalLabelPosition=bottom;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=center;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#39FF14;shape=mxgraph.azure.script_file;pointerEvents=1;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fontStyle=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="39" width="37.05" x="3688" y="-26920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-125" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=1;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;fillColor=default;gradientColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Sovereign Foundations&quot; — Primitive Throughput &amp;amp; Protocol Hygiene&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;In the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;.rice&lt;/b&gt; architecture, the &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;31&quot;&gt;util&lt;/code&gt; benchmarks represent the measurement of &quot;Molecular Stability.&quot; Before the system can enforce complex sovereign laws, its most basic operations—hexadecimal decoding and protocol framing—must operate at near-theoretical hardware limits. This benchmark suite ensures that the utility layer provides a zero-lag foundation for the higher-level &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;375&quot;&gt;CLERK&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;385&quot;&gt;MINT&lt;/b&gt; modules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Core Pillars of Sovereign Foundation Benchmarking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Hexadecimal Transformation Velocity (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;37&quot;&gt;decode_hex&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This measures the latency of converting raw string data into the internal byte format used by the sovereign kernel. By benchmarking this at the nanosecond level, we ensure that data ingestion—whether from a NATS stream or a local config—does not become a bottleneck for the system&#39;s reactive reflexes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Deterministic Protocol Framing (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;32&quot;&gt;proto_frame&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The benchmark for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;64&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;length_delimited_frame_byte_count&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; verifies the overhead of the system&#39;s communication protocol. It ensures that the logic used to &quot;slice&quot; and &quot;box&quot; messages for the Dual Kernel bridge is optimized for high-frequency messaging, providing a predictable performance floor for all inter-module communication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The &quot;Smoke Test&quot; Rapid Audit (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;30&quot;&gt;smoke_rows&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Beyond standard statistical benchmarking, the &quot;Smoke&quot; workload provides a lightweight, real-time metric of utility health. It allows the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;180&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Builder&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; to perform a &quot;Pre-Flight&quot; check of the system&#39;s primitive operations, ensuring that fundamental logic hasn&#39;t regressed before committing to a full sovereign build.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Compiler-Invariant Measurement (&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;32&quot;&gt;black_box&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Through the use of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;63&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;black_box&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; markers, the suite prevents the LLVM optimizer from making unrealistic assumptions about constant values. This guarantees that the measured performance reflects real-world execution where data is unpredictable and non-constant.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="520" width="600" x="3720" y="-26840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-147" edge="1" parent="1" source="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-122" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;shape=connector;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;strokeColor=#39FF14;strokeWidth=2;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=default;endArrow=classic;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;" target="PHxiAXBZ9Zwz3M3vVkmd-115">
